-- Updated Virgo entries — planet-specific
DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE sign = 'Virgo';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES

('Sun', 'Virgo', 'Your core identity is built on being useful, competent, and reliable. You''re driven to refine yourself and master practical skills, with a quiet confidence that comes from knowing your worth through what you deliver.', 'You naturally gravitate toward work that requires precision and care — you''re the person who notices what others miss and fixes it before anyone asks. Your life unfolds through service and self-improvement, constantly learning better ways to do things. You take pride in your effectiveness and your modest, understated way of making things better.', 'You''re most comfortable with people who appreciate your thoughtfulness and don''t mistake your critical nature for coldness. You show love through practical support and genuine interest in how others can improve. Your humility can be misread as low self-esteem, but it''s actually deep self-awareness.', 'Your perfectionism can paralyze you — waiting until conditions are perfect before you act or celebrate. You risk becoming so focused on problems that you miss the beauty of what''s working. Your self-criticism can be harsh enough to undermine your confidence.', 'Learn that competence isn''t about flawlessness; it''s about showing up and doing your best with what you have. Practice celebrating small wins instead of hunting for flaws. Your gift is seeing what needs healing — use it to help others, not just to police yourself.', 'Parker, "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"; Arroyo, "Astrology, Karma & Transformation"'),

('Moon', 'Virgo', 'Your emotional world is quiet and organized — you process feelings by analyzing them, sorting them into categories, and finding practical solutions. You need to feel useful and needed to feel emotionally secure.', 'You comfort yourself through routine, helpful action, and clear thinking; sitting with raw emotion without trying to fix it feels unbearable. You''re the steady presence others turn to in a crisis because you don''t fall apart, but you can get stuck in your own worry loops. Your emotional security comes from competence and having your life in working order.', 'You''re deeply loyal but can seem detached because you show care through doing things, not through emotional displays. You need people who understand that your constant suggestions come from genuine concern. A partner who respects your need for space and clarity feels like emotional safety.', 'You may suppress your feelings until they emerge as anxiety or harsh self-judgment. Your need to process everything intellectually can distance you from the wisdom of your gut instincts. You risk becoming so focused on others'' needs that you ignore your own emotional hunger.', 'Allow yourself to feel messy emotions without immediately organizing them away. Learn that vulnerability isn''t weakness — it''s the deepest form of honesty. Your analytical gifts are real, but emotional truth sometimes transcends logic.', 'Boulanger, "The Inner Sky"; Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"'),

('Mercury', 'Virgo', 'Your thinking is precise, methodical, and detail-obsessed — Mercury rules Virgo, so your mind is finely tuned to distinguish subtle differences and catch what others overlook. You''re less interested in grand theories and more interested in how things actually work.', 'You communicate with clarity and specificity; you''d rather say nothing than say something imprecise. You love research, categorization, and systems. Your communication style is direct and practical, focused on what''s useful and true. You''re the person colleagues trust to fact-check, to notice errors, and to explain complex things in understandable terms.', 'You''re drawn to people who appreciate intellectual precision and can engage in detailed conversation without taking it personally. You listen carefully and remember specifics others forget. Your communication partners need to understand that your questioning isn''t doubt — it''s discernment.', 'You can become so focused on accuracy that you lose sight of the bigger picture or come across as nitpicky. Your mind can get caught in worry loops about details that won''t matter in five years. You may struggle to speak up when you''re not 100% certain, silencing your valuable insights.', 'Develop confidence in your ability to communicate what you know, even with some uncertainty. Practice moving from analysis to decision-making; perfectionism isn''t accuracy. Your discriminating mind is a gift — trust it without needing every detail verified first.', 'Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"; Brady, "Predictive Astrology"'),

('Venus', 'Virgo', 'Your love style is modest, practical, and genuinely caring — but Venus is in fall here, so expressing affection feels awkward and overly analytical. You show love through thoughtful acts and genuine attention, not grand romantic gestures.', 'You''re attracted to people who are competent, intelligent, and honest about their flaws. You''re not impressed by surface charm; you need substance and real compatibility. In love, you express care by noticing details about the other person and offering genuine help. You''re most comfortable in relationships that feel like partnerships with room for personal growth.', 'You''re fiercely loyal but can seem cool or critical to those who need more overt affection and reassurance. Your tendency to point out what could be improved can feel harsh to lovers who want acceptance as they are. You may struggle to relax into romance or to receive love without immediately finding ways to improve the relationship.', 'Venus in fall makes it hard to trust that you''re lovable as you are — you believe you need to earn love through usefulness. You can be so focused on what''s wrong that you neglect celebration and pleasure. Your critical lens, while discerning, can make partners feel scrutinized rather than cherished.', 'Practice receiving compliments without pointing out your flaws. Learn that your partner loves you not for your utility but for who you are. Romance doesn''t need to be perfect to be real — sometimes the best love is quiet, consistent, and present.', 'Parker, "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"; Schulman, "Astrology of Self-Discovery"'),

('Mars', 'Virgo', 'Your drive is steady, methodical, and directed toward practical improvement — you''re not the flashy warrior type, but you have the endurance to accomplish real things. Your energy works best when you have clear goals and can see measurable progress.', 'You approach challenges by breaking them into manageable steps and working through them systematically. Your sexuality is more cerebral and detail-oriented; you need intellectual and emotional connection alongside physical attraction. You assert yourself through competence and clarity rather than aggression or dominance. You''re drawn to work that has real impact and visible results.', 'You''re dependable and follow through on commitments, which partners and collaborators appreciate deeply. You''re willing to do the unglamorous work that others avoid. Others sense that you''re genuinely interested in what actually works rather than what merely looks good.', 'Your reserved approach to action can make you hesitant in moments requiring bold risk-taking. You may channel your aggression into self-criticism or worry rather than outward assertion. Your need for perfect conditions can delay action until momentum is lost.', 'Develop trust in your ability to take imperfect action. Your methodical approach is a strength; don''t hold it back waiting for certainty. Learn to assert your needs directly instead of hoping others notice and fix things for you.', 'Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"; Arroyo, "Astrology, Karma & Transformation"'),

('Jupiter', 'Virgo', 'Your growth is quiet and built on genuine mastery — Jupiter is in detriment here, so expansion through overconfidence or excess doesn''t work for you. Your luck comes from doing excellent work and being trusted with responsibility.', 'You grow through service, learning, and gradually building expertise that others come to rely on. Your optimism is restrained and rooted in realistic assessment — you''re the person who says "we can do this because I''ve checked the details." You expand by deepening knowledge rather than chasing new shiny things. Opportunity finds you because of your reputation for reliability and competence.', 'People trust your counsel because you give practical, well-researched advice rather than empty inspiration. Your growth-oriented nature makes you a good mentor for those ready to actually do the work. Others sense that you genuinely want them to improve, not just to feel better temporarily.', 'The detriment of Jupiter here creates self-doubt about whether you''re enough — you always see how much more there is to learn. You may miss opportunities while perfecting your preparation. Your caution can look like lack of faith, limiting the scale of what you attempt.', 'Recognize that your growth is real, even when it''s incremental and quiet. Trust that doing good work is its own reward and opens doors you couldn''t predict. Stop waiting to be overqualified; stepping into challenges with good-faith effort is how expertise actually develops.', 'Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"; Schulman, "Astrology of Self-Discovery"'),

('Saturn', 'Virgo', 'Your life lessons are about building genuine competence and learning that self-mastery is freedom, not burden. Saturn is dignified here, so the discipline you develop becomes real strength rather than just self-imposed limitation.', 'You face lessons around perfectionism, guilt, and the belief that your worth depends on your usefulness. Your path involves learning to set boundaries, to stop fixing things that aren''t yours to fix, and to trust that resting isn''t laziness. Through these lessons, you build extraordinary reliability and integrity. You understand, in your bones, that integrity is the only foundation that lasts.', 'You attract people who need your steadiness and fear losing your support if they''re not perfect. You''re most compatible with those who understand that your boundaries come from self-respect, not rejection. Over time, you help others develop their own competence rather than depending on you.', 'You can internalize crushing amounts of responsibility and self-blame. Your critical voice can sound like Saturn, telling you you''re never good enough. You may deprive yourself of pleasure, rest, or celebration because they feel unearned. The weight of duty can calcify into rigidity.', 'Understand that discipline is strength, but perfectionism is prison. You''re already responsible — you don''t need to prove it anymore. Learn to say no to things that aren''t actually yours to carry. Real mastery includes knowing when to stop, rest, and trust others.', 'Parker, "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"; Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"'),

('Uranus', 'Virgo', 'Your generational rebellion is quiet but profound — you question existing systems by finding better, more efficient ways and proving your innovations work through evidence, not rhetoric. You''re the revolutionary who builds a better machine.', 'Your generation seeks to disrupt through refinement and optimization rather than destruction. You''re drawn to improving health systems, data systems, and service models. Your unique gifts come from seeing flaws in how things are organized and having the patience to redesign them properly. You push back against pointless rules and inefficiency through quiet, persistent alternatives.', 'You attract people who appreciate innovation grounded in reality and systems that actually work better. Your generation forms communities around practical solutions and shared commitment to doing things right. You''re most compatible with those who don''t need grand ideological declarations, just results.', 'Your quiet rebellion can be so understated that it''s overlooked, leading to frustration that your innovations aren''t adopted. You may rebel so subtly that you''re still locked in old patterns. The impulse to perfect things can become rebellion''s opposite — rigidity.', 'Trust that your innovations matter even when they don''t make headlines. Stop waiting for permission to implement your better ways. Your generation''s gift is proving that evolution works better than revolution — lean into that without losing your edge.', 'Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"; Arroyo, "Astrology, Karma & Transformation"'),

('Neptune', 'Virgo', 'Your generational spirituality is grounded and service-oriented — Neptune is in detriment here, so the transcendent and abstract must prove themselves through concrete help and healing. You seek the sacred in the practical and ordinary.', 'Your generation struggles with the gap between spiritual ideals and practical reality, but you''re learning to build spirituality that actually heals people. You''re drawn to meditation, bodywork, herbalism, and practical mysticism that you can understand and share. Your spiritual practice is unglamorous: showing up, paying attention, and serving without expectation of recognition.', 'You attract people seeking grounded spirituality and real healing rather than escapism. Your generation builds spiritual communities around actual help — food, medicine, counsel, presence. You find the sacred in clean water, good soil, and people being truly heard.', 'Neptune''s detriment can create disillusionment — you may feel spirituality should be more mystical and less practical. You can get so focused on earthly details that you lose the thread of meaning. Your rationality can become armor against the mystery you secretly crave.', 'Learn that the mundane is mystical — that presence itself is transcendence. Surrender to mystery without needing to understand or analyze it first. Your generation''s gift is building spirituality that actually works, that heals bodies and hearts, not just minds.', 'Parker, "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"; Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"'),

('Pluto', 'Virgo', 'Your generational transformation comes through deep scrutiny of systems, health, and how we organize work and service. You''re drawn to exposing hidden corruption and rebuilding based on truth and efficacy rather than tradition.', 'Your generation faces collective reckoning around work, perfection, health, and who gets to be invisible. You''re learning that transformation doesn''t require perfection — that broken systems must be understood in all their dysfunction before they can be rebuilt. Your power lies in seeing what''s been hidden or denied and having the courage to speak it.', 'You attract people ready for radical honesty about what''s not working — both personally and collectively. Your generation forms bonds through witnessing hard truths and building real alternatives. You''re compatible with those who understand that naming dysfunction is the first step of healing.', 'Pluto here can manifest as obsessive focus on what''s wrong — with yourself, your body, your systems. You may feel paralyzed by the scope of transformation needed. The pressure to be perfect can crack into destructive self-critique or harsh judgment of others'' imperfections.', 'Use your X-ray vision for healing, not just exposure. Transformation at this depth requires compassion — for yourself and those you''re trying to change. Your power isn''t in being pure; it''s in seeing clearly and staying committed to building something better.', 'Forrest, "The Twelve Houses"; Brady, "Predictive Astrology"');
